### The Anomaly Fusion Score — Why It Matters

This is the mathematical heart of our system. When a judge asks *"Why did your system decide this is a fault?"*, we show:

```
  Fusion Score: 0.82 (FAIL)
  
  Temporal ML:   0.88  ████████░░  (LSTM says this pattern is unusual)
  Physics:       0.79  ███████░░░  (dew point is physically inconsistent)
  Multivariate:  0.71  ███████░░░  (outlier in feature space)
  Context:       0.62  ██████░░░░  (unusual for this time/season)
  Edge QC:       1.00  ██████████  (rate-of-change exceeded)
  
  → Multiple independent signals agree. High confidence.
```

**No single point of failure.** One confused model can't cause a false alarm alone. The decision comes from agreement across independent detection approaches.

