## 7. The 6 Fault Types We Detect

| # | Fault | What It Looks Like | How We Catch It |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Spike** | Temperature: 32→33→**55**→34 | Rate-of-change check + LSTM temporal model |
| 2 | **Frozen** | Humidity: 67.2, 67.2, 67.2, 67.2... | Persistence counter + near-zero variance |
| 3 | **Drift** | Temperature slowly shifts +2°C over days | Trend analysis + LSTM baseline deviation |
| 4 | **Communication** | Missing data, NaN values, duplicate timestamps | Data integrity pattern detection |
| 5 | **Physical Inconsistency** | Values individually OK but combination is impossible | Physics engine (dew point, cross-variable) |
| 6 | **Range Violation** | Temperature = -80°C (physically impossible) | Hard range checks |

