### Why BME280?

One chip gives us ALL THREE required parameters (temperature + pressure + humidity) over a simple 2-wire I2C connection. Bosch-specified: ±3% RH accuracy, 300–1100 hPa pressure range, -40 to +85°C. Perfect for a prototype.

We frame it to judges as: *"We use BME280 as a compact prototype sensor node to reproduce the three required AWS variables"* — NOT as a professional IMD-grade sensor.

### Why Two BME280s?

Two sensors on the same ESP32 (different I2C addresses) lets us demonstrate **spatial consistency checking** physically:
- Corrupt one sensor → system detects which one is faulty by comparing with the other
- Judges can see this with their own eyes — much more convincing than a graph on screen

### Wiring (Simple)

```
ESP32 Pin 21 (SDA) ──→ shared data line for all I2C devices
ESP32 Pin 22 (SCL) ──→ shared clock line for all I2C devices
ESP32 3.3V         ──→ power for all modules
ESP32 GND          ──→ ground for all modules

BME280 #1: SDO → GND  (address 0x76)
BME280 #2: SDO → 3.3V (address 0x77)
```

